<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<rdf:RDF
         xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
         xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
         xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
         xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
         xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
         xmlns:games="https://example.org/schema/games">

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Homeworld">
         <games:number>1</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Homeworld is a real-time strategy video game developed by Relic Entertainment and published by Sierra Studios. It was released in 1999 and is known for its space-based sci-fi setting and 3D gameplay.
            The game's story revolves around a mothership and its fleet traveling through the galaxy.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Relic_Entertainment</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>1999-09-28</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS</games:platforms>  
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeworld"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Starcraft_II:_Wings_of_Liberty">
         <games:number>2</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            StarCraft II: Wings of Liberty is a science fiction real-time strategy video game developed and published by Blizzard Entertainment. It is the sequel to the 1998 video game StarCraft. 
            The game includes both new and returning characters and locations from the original game. The game was praised for its engaging single-player campaign and competitive multiplayer mode, making it a significant title in the esports industry.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Blizzard_Entertainment</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2010-07-27</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS</games:platforms>  
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/StarCraft_II:_Wings_of_Liberty"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/XCOM:_Enemy_Unknown">
         <games:number>3</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            XCOM: Enemy Unknown is a turn-based tactics video game developed by Firaxis Games and published by 2K Games. The game was released in 2012 and is a reimagining of the classic 1994 strategy game UFO: Enemy Unknown.
            It features a storyline involving an extraterrestrial invasion.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Firaxis_Games</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2012-10-09</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox 360, PlayStation 3</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XCOM:_Enemy_Unknown"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Halo_Wars">
         <games:number>4</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Halo Wars is a real-time strategy video game set in the Halo science fiction universe. It was developed by Ensemble Studios and published by Microsoft Game Studios. The game was released in 2009.
            It offers a unique take on the strategy genre within the context of the Halo franchise.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Ensemble_Studios</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2009-02-26</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Xbox 360, Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halo_Wars"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>  

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Sins_of_a_Solar_Empire">
         <games:number>5</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Sins of a Solar Empire is a real-time 4X strategy game developed by Ironclad Games and published by Stardock. The game was released in 2008 and takes place in a futuristic space setting with multiple factions vying for control.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Ironclad_Games</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2008-02-04</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sins_of_a_Solar_Empire"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>           
         
         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Endless_Space">
         <games:number>6</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Endless Space is a turn-based 4X strategy game developed by Amplitude Studios and published by Iceberg Interactive. The game was released in 2012 and is set in a fictional galaxy with multiple factions.
            It offers complex space exploration and empire management gameplay.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Amplitude_Studios</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2012-07-04</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endless_Space"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>           
         
         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Deus_Ex:_Mankind_Divided">
         <games:number>7</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Deus Ex: Mankind Divided is an action role-playing game with stealth and first-person shooter elements. Developed by Eidos-Montreal and published by Square Enix, the game was released in 2016.
            It is set in a dystopian cyberpunk future and offers players a mix of story-driven gameplay and strategic choices.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Eidos-Montreal</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2016-08-23</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox One, PlayStation 4</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deus_Ex:_Mankind_Divided"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>           
         
         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Supreme_Commander">
         <games:number>8</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Supreme Commander is a real-time strategy game developed by Gas Powered Games and published by THQ. The game was released in 2007 and is set in a future where different factions compete for control.
            It is known for its large-scale battles and strategic depth.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Gas_Powered_Games</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2007-02-20</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Commander"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>           
         
         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Stellaris">
         <games:number>9</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Stellaris is a grand strategy game developed by Paradox Development Studio and published by Paradox Interactive. The game was released in 2016 and is set in space.
            It focuses on empire building, exploration, and diplomacy in a sci-fi context.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Paradox_Development_Studio</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2016-05-09</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stellaris"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>           

         <games:scifi-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Alpha_Centauri">
         <games:number>10</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Sid Meier's Alpha Centauri is a 4X strategy game developed by Firaxis Games and published by Electronic Arts. The game was released in 1999 and is set in the future on an alien planet.
            It combines science fiction storytelling with strategy gameplay.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Firaxis_Games</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>1999-02-12</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_Centauri"/>
         </games:scifi-strategy>
</rdf:RDF>
